1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
During extreme weather, travelers may not
know which warning to trust

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
or where to find help. StormSignal brings
official warnings and local guidance together.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Chennai is our demo district. I’ll switch
between English, Tamil, and Hindi.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The main information and safety steps
change with the selected language.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The page shows the IMD district warning,
its exact wording, and the source update date.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Open the link to verify what the source
says.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
A scheduled refresh checks IMD’s public
Chennai page every 30 minutes.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
StormSignal displays the latest published
snapshot.

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,000
This is district-level forecast information,
not street-by-street flood reports.

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,000
The app does not show safe routes or
confirmed shelters.

11
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Safety steps reflect the warning category.

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
For thunder and lightning, go indoors,

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Avoid windows, and stay sheltered for
30 minutes after the last thunder.

14
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
If the source data is old or unavailable,
the app says it cannot verify the

15
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
current warning. No warning listed
is not an all-clear.

16
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Let’s open IMD’s page to compare its
wording and date, then return to the app.

17
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Now we’ll show the official local contacts.

18
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:04,000
The contact panel has tap-to-call links
for Chennai’s Disaster Helpline 1077

19
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,000
and Corporation 1913, with a link to
verify the numbers.

20
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:17,000
StormSignal helps travelers understand
official warnings in a familiar language.

21
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:25,000
In an emergency, follow local authority
instructions.
